{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: exact repaired identifiers (b) head de980a3d77145291de7b27e7e796974d8c963862 on builder/identifiers-vectors-b-20261110, all 25 artifacts, for request a30f1b67 under promise 5a78cc01 and review request 3e0f9278. The planner ruled in 864fd7bb that the stale mark on this set, which supersede ae9d8483 caused, is no finding. The repair closes the one change that review 8105f25b required. Replay's citation verifier now reads a Git commit's parents as Git does, and the independent vectors pin that rule.\n\nThe repair:\n\n- `gitEvent` (`packages/replay/src/citation.ts`) accepts `parent` headers only in the run directly after `tree`. It validates each parent digest and follows the first one. A `parent` header after any other header returns null, which `verifyCitation` reports as `mismatch`/`position`, reached 1. Git reads parents from the same run and ignores a later `parent` line. The verifier now never follows a parent that Git does not read, and it refuses the commits where the two readings could differ.\n- Sections 4, 7 and 8 of the protocol note state the rule and the refusal. The level-2 shell script in section 4 uses the same rule, and the note says that the corrected script has not run yet.\n- The producer adds one `parent-after-author` case for each Git format. The `git256` case cites `e1bed0b2…`, the exact object that my earlier probe built, and expects `mismatch`/`position`, reached 1, with a null anchor and empty trusts.\n\nWhat I checked, on my own extracted copy with no shared validation slot:\n\n- I ran `scripts/identifier-vectors.py` once with `python3 -I` into a new scratch directory. It produced 30, 27 and 27 cases and reproduced all six committed vector files byte for byte.\n- `packages/bytes/test/citation.test.ts` passes 2 of 2. `citation.test.ts`, `citation-git.test.ts` and `cli.test.ts` in Replay pass 13 of 13, and those 13 include the two new rows. `node --test scripts/security-entry-points.test.mjs scripts/security-settings.test.mjs` passes 15 of 15. The Bytes index seal stays `7c8c9514…`, and only its comment changes.\n- Scope. Main ab802614 is an ancestor, the head is pushed, and the builder's worktree is clean at the head. Against main, the head changes exactly the 25 paths that its 25 artifacts cover. From 8793316b to 7f06529a, only the five repair paths change. From 7f06529a to 3da82263, only the two Git case files change. From 3da82263 to the head, only the note and the descriptor change. `check-notes` reports 0 warnings. The commit-message check passes: 10 checked, 0 flagged. `git diff --check` is clean, and `check-doc-links.mjs` checks 1,238 local links and finds none broken.\n- Evidence. The 86 files in the descriptor match their SHA-256 values in `/Users/hughpyle/play/artroom-evidence/2026-11-11-identifiers-b-final-3da8226/unit`. `SHA256SUMS` verifies, and the aggregate manifest hashes to `4c49f9bc…de51`. The repair-focus summary records every exit 0 at 3da82263. The old-scan control records a negative child exit 1 with every enclosing exit 0. The earlier history stays under `history/377b/`, with the failed fa6 gate still recorded as failed.\n- CI. GitHub reports Page run 43099179105 and Card run 43099182682 as attempt 1, completed and successful, at the head. Both runs are manual dispatches, because the repair and documentation paths match neither workflow's push filter.\n- Ruling 15d3b0bd accepts the focused continuation for this repair in place of a second complete gate. The repair changes one private function whose only caller is `verifyCitation`, and the Page build at 7f06529a left `assets.ts` byte-equal at `e104ec88…0530`. I accept the no-call correspondence on that basis.\n\nArchitecture: sound. Citation integrity stays separate from Native judgment. Bytes parses citations, and Replay verifies them and reads byte sources. The CLI mode is separate, and the Native argv keeps its meaning. Identifiers (c+d) still owns the Native identity, admission, archive and wire cutover.\n\nSecurity: no finding. The finding in review 8105f25b is fixed, and two independent vector rows plus the old-scan control pin it. Option errors throw before I/O. Byte sources are bounded at 8 MiB. Git runs fixed commands with a 10-second timeout and a scrubbed environment, with no replace refs or lazy fetch. SHA-1 hashing runs in a fresh empty directory with no `-w`. Fetched bytes never become anchors.\n\nSimplification: no required change. The two notes from review 8105f25b are taken: the seal comment now names the citation parser exports, and the note states the `incomplete`/`unavailable` answer for a duplicate digest claim.\n\nThis approval authorizes no deployment, cutover or live acceptance. The planner decides the landing.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:c71ecb886b494118e3cf9141a1d668a48a87b059","binding":"assigned","head":"de980a3d77145291de7b27e7e796974d8c963862","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:10cbb8dcb6faff062f78d6935a34d9d346ac18ef\",\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:ede60bc13617ec56483276dfa72312606549bf10\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:5a78cc018bfd89dbcd0b6882645b8ca8225455ec\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:6745baa96a2e7d32f0d5e2a34a0ba2a163231039","review_path":"reviewguard@1","stale":"true","stale_bases":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:10cbb8dcb6faff062f78d6935a34d9d346ac18ef, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:26d1dc15ebd0080eb5ad8e6c52b70b0a9ef35527, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:27c5cfb00e1513bba8fb5a87fc77828afca221a2, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:2a9a24f2ad5dad5bc692106f822d5fcf126d9c80, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:2bca43b38422885cb4334f9a0f1b3d92722e9c8d, git:sha